proof.text:
Step 1 gives $K\in D^+$ and step 3 gives $Q=Rj_*K\in D^{[a,b+d]}$. The morphism $j$ is qcqs by step 2. The bounded-below comparison theorem therefore identifies $Rj_{\mathrm{proét},*}
u_U^*K$ with $
u_X^*Q$. Apply the comparison Tor-interval theorem to the finite commutative ring $A$, the bounded-below étale object $Q$, and the interval $[a,b+d]$ (nonempty since $d\ge0$). By clause (2) its étale Tor-amplitude hypothesis holds, and the theorem gives the same bound against every pro-étale module sheaf. For every pro-étale module sheaf $N$, tensor the displayed isomorphism with $N$ and take cohomology. This identifies each $\mathcal H^r(Rj_{\mathrm{proét},*}
u_U^*K\otimes_A^{\mathbf L}N)$ with $\mathcal H^r(
u_X^*Q\otimes_A^{\mathbf L}N)$, which vanishes for $r
otin[a,b+d]$. This proves clause (3).
